xemu-xbox (0.8.136-1foundry2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Rename xemu -> xemu-xbox. Two unrelated upstreams are both called "xemu";
    LGB's 8-bit emulator suite has shipped its own .deb under that name since
    2016, so the bare name goes to it and this package is qualified. Removes a
    dpkg identity collision in which that upstream's self-built .deb would
    silently replace this one.
  * The installed binary is unchanged and remains /usr/bin/xemu — only the
    package name is qualified, so there is no file conflict with xemu.
  * No transitional package: there are no existing consumers, and the old
    artifacts are dropped from the repository rather than superseded.

 -- Foundry Linux <packages@foundrylinux.org>  Wed, 05 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0700

xemu (0.8.136-1foundry1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial Foundry Linux package of xemu, the original Xbox emulator.
  * Built from the upstream v0.8.136 release source archive
    (xemu-0.8.136.tar.zst), which vendors the meson subprojects that the
    plain git tag archive omits.
  * Packaging written from scratch rather than adopting upstream's in-tree
    debian/ directory: that tree is inherited from Debian's QEMU packaging
    and is stale (changelog frozen at 0.5.2/2021, debhelper compat 11,
    Standards-Version 3.9.8, d/watch pointing at download.qemu.org, and a
    d/copyright describing QEMU rather than xemu).
  * Add a section-1 man page (Debian Policy 12.1); upstream ships none.
  * Add the runtime libraries that the vendored SDL3 dlopens (libvulkan1, the
    X11 client set, EGL/GL/GBM/DRM) to Depends, plus Vulkan ICD and audio
    backends to Recommends. dh_shlibdeps cannot see a dlopen, so without this
    the package installed but failed to start for lack of a Vulkan loader.
  * Install the AppStream metainfo as app.xemu.xemu.metainfo.xml so the
    filename matches the component id (appstreamcli validate-tree).
  * Honour DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=parallel=N instead of calling nproc.

 -- Foundry Linux <packages@foundrylinux.org>  Wed, 05 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
